# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [SPANK plugin](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) for "
"the [Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) is used to "
"configure access to quantum resources from user jobs in a compute "
"environment administrated by the "
"[Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html) workload manager. It "
"handles the acquisition and release of access to quantum resources and sets "
"the necessary environment variables for executing quantum workloads. The "
"available quantum resources are specified in a `qrmi_config.json` file, "
"which is managed by an administrator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [SPANK plugin](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) para "
"sa [Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) ay ginagamit"
" para i-configure ang access sa mga quantum resource mula sa mga user job sa"
" isang compute environment na pinapamahalaan ng "
"[Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html) workload manager. "
"Hinahawakan nito ang pagkuha at paglabas ng access sa mga quantum resource, "
"at itinatakda ang mga kinakailangang environment variable para sa "
"pagpapatakbo ng mga quantum workload. Ang mga available na quantum resource "
"ay tinukoy sa isang `qrmi_config.json` na file, na pinapamahalaan ng isang "
"administrator.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once installed, this plugin registers the following option. A Slurm user can"
" specify which quantum resources are used for the Slurm job script.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag na-install na, irerehistro ng plugin na ito ang sumusunod na opsyon. "
"Maaaring tukuyin ng isang Slurm user kung aling mga quantum resource ang "
"gagamitin para sa Slurm job script.\n"

