msgid ""
"For the allocator node, your don't need to specify the path to "
"qrmi_config.json, as in the following.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa allocator node, hindi mo na kailangang tukuyin ang path sa "
"qrmi_config.json, tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following table shows which Slurm context nodes these files should be copied to. For more details of each context, refer to the [documentation](https://slurm.schedmd.com/spank.html#SECTION_SPANK-PLUGINS) for the SPANK plugin.\n"
"| Files | Slurm contexts |\n"
"| ------- | ------- |\n"
"| `plugstack.conf` | **local**, **remote**, **allocator**, **slurmd**, and **job_script** |\n"
"| `qrmi_config.json` | **remote** (Compute nodes) |\n"
"| `spank_qrmi.so` | **allocator** and **remote** (Login nodes and compute nodes) |\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na talahanayan ay nagpapakita kung aling mga Slurm context node ang dapat kopyahan ng mga file na ito. Para sa karagdagang detalye ng bawat context, tingnan ang [dokumentasyon](https://slurm.schedmd.com/spank.html#SECTION_SPANK-PLUGINS) para sa SPANK plugin.\n"
"| Mga File | Mga Slurm context |\n"
"| ------- | ------- |\n"
"| `plugstack.conf` | **local**, **remote**, **allocator**, **slurmd**, at **job_script** |\n"
"| `qrmi_config.json` | **remote** (Mga compute node) |\n"
"| `spank_qrmi.so` | **allocator** at **remote** (Mga login node at compute node) |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Once `plugstack.conf` is updated, SPANK plugins will be loaded at runtime during the next job launch, which means administrators do not need to restart the Slurm cluster.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Kapag na-update na ang `plugstack.conf`, ang mga SPANK plugin ay ilo-load sa runtime sa susunod na paglulunsad ng job, ibig sabihin hindi na kailangang i-restart ng mga administrator ang Slurm cluster.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

